<title>USA: Marathon Oil raises U.S. posted crude prices.</title>
<headline>Marathon Oil raises U.S. posted crude prices.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Marathon Oil, a unit of USX Corp, said it raised the price it will pay for U.S. crude oil by 75 cents a barrel, effective December 13.</p>
<p>The increase brings the new price for U.S. benchmark grade West Texas Intermediate to $22.75 a barrel, and West Texas Sour to $21.40 a barrel.</p>
<p>Light Louisiana sweet crude is now $22.75 a barrel, and Oklahoma sweet is $23.25.</p>
<p>-- New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859-1620</p>
